913	\section{Introduction}
914	The Left Right Symmetric Model (LRSM)~\cite{Pati:1974yy,Mohapatra:1974gc,Senjanovic:1975rk} 
915	is an economic and well-defined solution to a number discrepancies within the Standard Model of particle physics (SM).
916	 Such issues include: the origin and lightness of neutrino masses, the existence of dark matter, and 
917	the baryon-antibaryon asymmetry of the universe.
918	
919	The model, based on the gauge group
920	\begin{equation}
921	 {\rm SU}(3)_c \otimes {\rm SU}(2)_L \otimes {\rm SU}(2)_R \otimes {\rm U}(1)_{B-L},
922	\end{equation}
923	predicts {right-handed (RH) currents and the existence of heavy, RH gauge bosons $W_R^\pm$ and $Z_R$. In addition,} the model contains 
924	 three RH neutrinos $N_R$ that are charged under ${\rm SU}(2)_R \otimes {\rm U}(1)_{B-L}$ but singlets under SM symmetries.
925	For masses up to several TeV, the LRSM can be tested at {collider experiments such as the Large Hadron Collider (LHC)}  through searches for processes like
926	\begin{eqnarray}
927	 p ~p \rightarrow	& \WR^\pm	& \rightarrow tb ~\text{or}~ N_R \ell^\pm, ~
928	 \quad\text{with}\quad N_R \rightarrow 	\ell^\pm W_R^{\mp *}  \rightarrow \ell^\pm q \overline{q'},
929	 \quad\text{and}
930	 \label{eq:ppWRff}
931	 \\
932	 p ~p \rightarrow	& \ZR		& \rightarrow t\overline{t} ~\text{or}~ N_R N_R,
933	 \quad\text{with}\quad \ell \in\{e,\mu,\tau\}, \quad q\in\{u,c,d,s,t,b\},
934	  \label{eq:ppZRff}
935	\end{eqnarray}
936	and are shown diagrammatically in Fig.~\ref{fig:production}.
937	The channels lead to {the distinct}  
938	$\ell^\pm\ell^\pm +nj$~\cite{Keung:1983uu}, $\ell^\pm+j$~\cite{Ferrari:2000sp,Mitra:2016kov}, and single top~\cite{Simmons:1996ws} topologies, 
939	and have been studied 
940	extensively~\cite{Han:2012vk,Chen:2013fna,Vasquez:2014mxa,Ng:2015hba,Dev:2015kca,Kang:2015uoc,FileviezPerez:2016erl,
941	  Frank:2010cj,Tello:2010am, Das:2012ii,  Maiezza:2015lza,Gluza:2015goa,Chakrabortty:2016wkl,Ferrari:2000sp,Mitra:2016kov,Simmons:1996ws}.
942	
943	
944	
945	
946	
947	
948	\begin{figure}[!t]
949	\begin{center}
950	\subfigure[]{\includegraphics[scale=1,width=.48\textwidth]{feynman_qq_WR_ff.eps}	\label{fig:feynmanWR}}
951	\subfigure[]{\includegraphics[scale=1,width=.48\textwidth]{feynman_qq_ZR_ff.eps}	\label{fig:feynmanZR}}
952	\end{center}
