1019	\section{Effective Left-Right Symmetric Model}\label{sec:theory}
1020	The Effective LRSM field content consists of the usual SM states, the $\WR^\pm$ and $\ZR$ gauge bosons, 
1021	which are aligned with their mass eigenstates, and three heavy Majorana neutrinos $N_i$, 
1022	aligned with the RH chiral states.
1023	
1024	In the LRSM, the $\WR$ chiral coupling to quarks are given by
1025	\begin{eqnarray}
1026	 \mathcal{L}_{\WR-q-q'} = \frac{-\kappa_R^q g}{\sqrt{2}}\sum_{i,j=u,d,\dots}\overline{u}_i V_{ij}^{\rm CKM'}~W_{R \mu}^+ \gamma^\mu P_R~ d_j + \text{H.c.},
1027	 \label{chcurrent}
1028	\end{eqnarray}
1029	Here, $u_i (d_j)$ is an up-(down-)type quark of flavor $i (j)$; 
1030	$P_{R(L)} = \frac{1}{2}(1\pm\gamma^5)$ denotes the RH(LH) chiral projection operator; and
1031	$V_{ij}^{\rm CKM'}$  is the RH Cabbibo-Kobayashi-Masakawa (CKM) matrix, which is related to the SM CKM matrix.
1032	Throughout this study, we will assume five massless quarks and take both the SM and RH CKM matrices to be diagonal with unit entries.
1033	$g=\sqrt{4\pi\alpha_{\rm EM}(M_Z)}/\sin\theta_W$ is the SM Weak coupling constant and 
1034	$\kappa_{R}^{q}\in\mathds{R}$ is an overall normalization for the $\WR$ interaction strength.
1035	
1036	For leptons, the $\WR$ coupling and leptonic mixing is parametrized by~\cite{Atre:2009rg,Han:2012vk}
1037	\begin{eqnarray}
1038	 \mathcal{L}_{\WR-\ell-\nu/N} = \frac{-\kappa_R^\ell g}{\sqrt{2}}
1039	 \sum_{\ell=e,\mu,\tau}
1040	 \left[
1041	 \sum_{m=1}^3	\overline{\nu^{c}_m} X_{\ell m} ~+~
1042	 \sum_{m'=1}^3	\overline{N_{m'}} Y_{\ell m'}
1043	 \right] ~W_{R \mu}^+ \gamma^\mu P_R~ \ell^-+\text{H.c.}
1044	\end{eqnarray}
1045	The matrix $Y_{\ell m'} (X_{\ell m})$ quantifies the mixing between 
1046	the heavy (light) neutrino mass eigenstate $N_{m'}~(\nu_{m})$
1047	and the RH chiral state with corresponding lepton flavor $\ell$. 
1048	
1049	The mixing scale as~\cite{Keung:1983uu}
1050	\begin{equation}
1051	\vert Y_{\ell m'}\vert^2 \sim \mathcal{O}(1) \quad\text{and}\quad  
1052	\vert X_{\ell m}\vert^2 \sim 1 - \vert Y_{\ell m'}\vert^2 \sim \mathcal{O}(m_{\nu_m}/m_{N_{m'}}).
1053	\end{equation}
1054	As in the quark sector, $\kappa_R^\ell\in\mathds{R}$ independently normalizes the $\WR$ coupling strength to leptons.
1055	
1056	At TeV collider scales, both light neutrino masses and light neutrino mixing can be taken to zero.
1057	So for simplicity, we take $Y_{\ell m'}$ to  be diagonal with unit entires:
1058	\begin{equation}
1059	  \vert Y_{e N}\vert = \vert Y_{\mu N_2}\vert = \vert Y_{\tau N_3}\vert = 1, \quad \vert Y_{\rm others}\vert = \vert X_{\ell m}\vert = 0.
1060	  \label{eq:lrsmNuMixing}
1061	\end{equation}
1062	
1063	Mass and mixing assumptions are modifiable in the public model files~\cite{nloFRModel} but requires UFO regeneration.
1064	Specifically, do not load the FR restrictions, ``massless.rst'' and ``diagonalCKM.rst''.
1065	
1066	
1067	
